OL,3,ABrazil's Congress approves shorter
OL,4,Aworking week in win for Lula
OL,5,
OL,6,FBrazil's Congress has approved a
OL,7,Fconstitutional amendment that will cut
OL,8,Fthe working week from 44 hours to 40
OL,9,Fand give employees two days off per
OL,10,Fweek without cutting their salary.
OL,12,FThe change represents the biggest
OL,13,Foverhaul to workers' rights since
OL,14,FBrazil's return to democracy in 1988.
OL,16,FSenators passed the amendment, which
OL,17,Fleft-wing President Luiz Inacio Lula da
OL,18,FSilva had championed, less than two
OL,19,Fweeks before a second round in the
OL,20,FLatin American nation's presidential
OL,21,Felection.
OL,23,APub: 15-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
